  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V2X Systems has $794M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. V2X Systems won 533 awards this year, with an average award size of $1.5M, and obligations fell 53.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is by far the largest buyer, obligating $761M. Facilities Support Services is the dominant market for V2X Systems, accounting for $696M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations peaked in FY23 at $2B and have since moved to $1.6B in FY24, $1.7B in FY25, and $794M in FY26 so far. Other notable markets include Engineering Services at $33.7M, Communication Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $20.8M, and All Other Telecommunications at $17.3M. The Department of State, Department of Health and Human Services, and Department of Homeland Security are smaller buyers, with obligations of $31.6M, $1.5M, and $377K respectively. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year results.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are V2X Systems' top buyers this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $761M from V2X Systems in FY2026 to date. The Department of State obligated $31.6M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $1.5M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $377K. Those four agencies make up the top buying agencies listed for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive V2X Systems' federal revenue?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services is the largest market for V2X Systems at $696M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services accounted for $33.7M, Communication Equipment Repair and Maintenance accounted for $20.8M, and All Other Telecommunications accounted for $17.3M. Smaller markets include Other Computer Related Services at $10.1M and Landscape Architectural Services at $10M."
      }
    ]
